+ Response 204 (application/json)

### Remove a Package Owner [DELETE]

+ Request

    This request requires authentication.

    + Header

            Authorization: e2bfe5e65b9235acebe06df8027905c0

+ Response 204

# Group API Keys

API Keys are used to authenticate requests (see Authentication section for more details). A key has a name used to identify it and a secret that is used for the actual authentication.

Only a user who signed in can create or revoke keys. The request must authenticate with an OAuth token from the Device Authorization Grant. The server refuses API tokens and OAuth tokens from the Client Credentials Grant with `403 Forbidden`, so a leaked key cannot create keys that outlive it or revoke other keys.

Each key has a list of permissions. A permission has a `domain` and, for some domains, a `resource`:

| Domain | Resource | Allows |
|--------|----------|--------|
| `api` | none, `read`, or `write` | `read`: all API reads. `write` or none: all API actions, which includes all write domains below |
| `package` | `NAME` or `REPOSITORY/NAME` | Publish and change owners of one package, and all API reads |
| `publish` | none, `NAME`, or `REPOSITORY/NAME` | Publish, revert, retire, and unretire releases, and publish documentation. With a resource, only for that package |
| `owners` | none, `NAME`, or `REPOSITORY/NAME` | Add and remove package owners. With a resource, only for that package |
| `members` | none | Add, remove, and change the role of organization members |
| `administration` | none | Change the number of seats of an organization |
| `repository` | `ORGANIZATION` | Fetch from the private repository of the organization. Only for organization keys |
| `repositories` | none | Fetch from all private repositories the owner can access. Only for organization keys |
| `docs` | `ORGANIZATION` | Fetch private documentation of the organization |

The server refuses the `keys` domain. A key is limited by what its owner can do when the key is used. For an organization key, the role of the member who creates the key also limits which permissions the key can get.

## API Keys Collection [/keys]

### List all API Keys [GET]

+ Request

    This request requires authentication.

    + Header

            Accept: application/json
            Authorization: e2bfe5e65b9235acebe06df8027905c0

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Attributes (array[API Key])

    + Body

            [{
              "name": "my_computer",
              "authing_key": true,
              "token_format": "v1",
              "permissions": [
                {
                  "domain": "api",
                  "resource": "read"
                }
              ],
              "revoke_at": null,
              "last_use": {
                "ip": "192.168.1.1",
                "user_agent": "Hex/2.0.0 (Elixir/1.14.0) (OTP/25.0)",
                "used_at": "2014-04-21T18:00:00Z"
              },
              "inserted_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "updated_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "url": "https://hex.pm/api/keys/my_computer"
            }]

### Create an API Key [POST]

+ Request

    This request requires an OAuth token from the Device Authorization Grant. It is allowed to be made even if the account email has not yet been confirmed. A user with two-factor authentication must send the `x-hex-otp` header.

    + Attributes
        + `name` (string, required)
        + `permissions` (array, optional) - List of permissions for the key
        + `revoke_at` (string, optional) - ISO8601-encoded timestamp when the key should be automatically revoked. Must be in the future.

    + Header

            Accept: application/json
            Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
            x-hex-otp: 123456

    + Body

            {
              "name": "my_computer",
              "permissions": [
                {
                  "domain": "api",
                  "resource": "write"
                }
              ],
              "revoke_at": "2024-05-21T17:20:12Z"
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

    The `secret` will be sent only once. It should be stored after creating the API key. Subsequent responses to GET requests will not include the `secret`.

    + Attributes (API Key)
        + `secret` - The key secret

    + Header

            Location: https://hex.pm/api/keys/my_computer

    + Body

            {
              "name": "my_computer",
              "secret": "hex_e2bfe5e65b9235acebe06df8027905c09a3b1c2d",
              "authing_key": false,
              "token_format": "v2",
              "permissions": [
                {
                  "domain": "api",
                  "resource": "write"
                }
              ],
              "revoke_at": "2024-05-21T17:20:12Z",
              "inserted_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "updated_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "url": "https://hex.pm/api/keys/my_computer"
            }

### Remove all API Keys [DELETE]

Removes all API keys for the authenticated user.

+ Request

    This request requires an OAuth token from the Device Authorization Grant. A user with two-factor authentication must send the `x-hex-otp` header.

    + Header

            Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
            x-hex-otp: 123456

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body

            null

+ Response 403 (application/json)

    The request authenticated with an API token.

    + Body

            {
              "status": 403,
              "message": "API keys cannot revoke API keys, revoke the key on https://hex.pm/dashboard/keys"
            }

## API Key [/keys/{name}]

+ Parameters
    + name: my_computer (string)
        Key name

+ Attributes
    + `name` (string, required) - Key name
    + `secret` (string, optional) - Only available immediately after creation, the user secret for the key
    + `authing_key` (boolean, required) - Whether this key is the one being used for the current request
    + `token_format` (enum[string], required) - Format of the secret
        + Members
            + `v1` - 32 hex characters without a prefix
            + `v2` - `hex_` prefix
    + `permissions` (array, required) - List of permissions the key has
      + (object)
        + `domain` (enum[string], required) - The domain of the permission
            + Members
                + `api` - Gives permission to actions on the API (can be specified with `resource` values `write` and `read`, default is `write`)
                + `repository` - Gives permission to actions on a specific repository specified in the `resource`
                + `repositories` -  Gives permission to actions on all repositories the user has access to, the `resource` is omitted
                + `package` - Gives permission to publish and change owners of the package specified in the `resource`, and to all API reads
                + `publish` - Gives permission to publish, revert, retire, and unretire releases, optionally only for the package specified in the `resource`
                + `owners` - Gives permission to add and remove package owners, optionally only for the package specified in the `resource`
                + `members` - Gives permission to manage organization members, the `resource` is omitted
                + `administration` - Gives permission to change the number of seats of an organization, the `resource` is omitted
                + `docs` - Gives permission to fetch private documentation of the organization specified in the `resource`
        + `resource` (string, optional)
    + `revoke_at` (string, optional) - If set, the ISO8601-encoded timestamp when the key will be automatically revoked
    + `last_use` (object, optional) - Information about the last time this key was used
        + `used_at` (string, required) - ISO8601-encoded timestamp
        + `ip` (string, required) - IP address of the request
        + `user_agent` (string, required) - User-Agent header of the request
    + `inserted_at` (string, required) - ISO8601-encoded timestamp
    + `updated_at` (string, required) - ISO8601-encoded timestamp
    + `url` (string, required)

### Fetch an API Key [GET]

+ Request

    This request requires authentication.

    + Header

            Accept: application/json
            Authorization: e2bfe5e65b9235acebe06df8027905c0

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Attributes (API Key)

    + Body

            {
              "name": "my_computer",
              "authing_key": true,
              "token_format": "v1",
              "permissions": [
                {
                  "domain": "api",
                  "resource": "write"
                }
              ],
              "revoke_at": null,
              "last_use": {
                "ip": "192.168.1.1",
                "user_agent": "Hex/2.0.0 (Elixir/1.14.0) (OTP/25.0)",
                "used_at": "2014-04-21T18:00:00Z"
              },
              "inserted_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "updated_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "url": "https://hex.pm/api/keys/my_computer"
            }

### Remove an API Key [DELETE]

+ Request

    This request requires an OAuth token from the Device Authorization Grant. The server refuses API tokens with `403 Forbidden`. A user with two-factor authentication must send the `x-hex-otp` header.

    + Header

            Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
            x-hex-otp: 123456

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    Returns the revoked key.

    + Attributes (API Key)

    + Body

            {
              "name": "my_computer",
              "authing_key": false,
              "token_format": "v1",
              "permissions": [
                {
                  "domain": "api",
                  "resource": "write"
                }
              ],
              "revoke_at": null,
              "inserted_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "updated_at": "2014-04-21T17:20:12Z",
              "url": "https://hex.pm/api/keys/my_computer"
            }

